Liquid Metal ("Warped Liquid Metal") by Mårten Rånge (mrange)
https://www.shadertoy.com/view/3t2czh

The author's notice in the shader reads: "Licence CC0: Liquid Metal"

Where it is stated: the first comment line of the shader's own source (after
the lines "// url: https://www.shadertoy.com/view/3t2czh" and "// credits:
mrange"), as copied in
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y4my4my4m/kde-shader-wallpaper/HEAD/package/contents/ui/Shaders/Warped_LiquidMetal.frag
(line 4), and the same words open the shader's description on Shadertoy
(checked in the Shadertoy API record for shader 3t2czh, mirrored at
https://github.com/GabeRundlett/shadertoy-api-shaders/blob/master/shaders/3t2czh.json,
author "mrange"; the Shadertoy web page itself could not be fetched by script).
The two copies of the code are identical. The GPL-3.0 licence of the KDE
wallpaper repository that bundles the file does not cover this shader; the
author's own CC0 notice does.

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper; see the note at the
top of main.metal for what was changed:
  - the GLSL out/inout parameters of rot() and mainImage() are written as
    thread references;
  - the animation runs at half speed (iTime is read as iTime * 0.5), because the
    original's warp churns quickly for a desktop background.
The algorithm, constants and lighting are otherwise untouched. No images are
shipped.

Provenance note. The shader's comments credit one outside influence: normal()
says "As suggested by IQ, thanks!", a technique suggested by Inigo Quilez, with
no code attributed. Separately, vnoise() is built the way Inigo Quilez's
published value-noise code is (quintic fade, four hashed lattice corners, the
k0/k1/k2 expansion; compare https://www.shadertoy.com/view/4dXBRH). The author
does not say he copied it and the construction is textbook, but in case any of
it derives from that work, Inigo Quilez published it under the MIT License:

